# REQUIRES: haydn-registered-target
# RUN: llc -mtriple=haydn-unknown-elf -mcpu=haydn -x mir \
# RUN:   -start-before=haydn-expand-pseudos \
# RUN:   -stop-after=haydn-late-convergence -o - %s | FileCheck %s

# CB-167 chained read-old dissolve. skip3.mir is
# { dead LD r9 ; dead SRAI r8 ; ADD killed r8, killed r9 }; ADD is a third
# GPR write, so S1's product 2W probe sequentializes the shell before
# first S2 can reopen it. The live pin keeps that chained shape with a
# 0W store reader so S1 commits the 3-member parcel and first S2
# (bumpPostRASchedInvocation()==2) actually walks the CB-167 Order splice.
#
# Intra-cycle RAW skips dead defs (snapshot read-old). Reopen must splice
# every colliding dead-def AFTER its last same-parcel reader and must not
# skip the member that shifts into the vacated slot. A for-I auto-increment
# after erase+insert leaves SRAI before the store; the rebuilt DAG then
# serializes SRAI then ST and the store writes NEW r8 instead of the
# livein/old value.
#
# Store/load same-cycle overlap sequentializes unproven pairs and leaves
# a hole the ALU dead-def fills (SRAI in the load packet, store later).
# Load @s / store @t are distinct identified objects: AA NoAlias (and
# not TII same-base) keeps the 3-member so dissolve still walks it.
# Same-object overlap is the d110 pin, not this one. Do not change
# LateConvergence dissolve to restore this CHECK.
#
# Product sms2 stays ON (do not pass -haydn-sms2=0). The pin starts
# before ExpandPseudos so S1 then first S2 actually run. Limited
# -start-before pipelines skip post-S2 Finalize (stall NOP stays
# logical); stop after late-convergence to observe dissolve order.

--- |
  target triple = "haydn-unknown-unknown-elf"
  @s = internal global i32 0
  @t = internal global i32 0
  define void @f(i32 %k, ptr %p, i32 %one) { ret void }
...
---
name:            f
tracksRegLiveness: true
noVRegs:         true
body:             |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $r4, $r6, $r8, $r9
    BUNDLE 1, 0, implicit-def dead $r9, implicit-def dead $r8, implicit $r6, implicit $r4, implicit killed $r8, implicit killed $r9 :: (volatile dereferenceable load (s32) from @s) {
      dead $r9 = S_LW_WITH_IMM_E3_E1_LOAD1_RI6 $r6, 0 :: (volatile dereferenceable load (s32) from @s)
      dead $r8 = SRAI32_E3_E2_ALU2_RI5 $r4, 2
      S_SW_WITH_IMM_E3_E0_LOADSTORE0_RI6 killed $r8, killed $r9, 0 :: (volatile store (s32) into @t)
    }
    $r0 = JALR_E2_E0_ALU0_RI12 $r15, 0

# Store must sample PRIOR r8/r9 (liveins). Sequential SRAI-before-store is
# the skip defect. Same-line coissue with the store matched before srai32
# is still legal snapshot read-old. CHECK-NOT is the region before the
# store, so srai32 later on the same packet still passes.
# CHECK-NOT: SRAI32
# CHECK: S_SW_WITH_IMM{{.*}}$r8, killed $r9
